# Billing & Stripe

SDK: `stripe@^22.0.2`. Initialised lazily in `src/lib/stripe.ts`:

```ts
// Note the absence of apiVersion — pinning broke against v22 types.
new Stripe(process.env.STRIPE_SECRET_KEY!);
```

`isBillingEnabled()` returns `Boolean(STRIPE_SECRET_KEY)`. Routes that don't degrade gracefully when Stripe is off must check this and 503 with a clear message.

## Plans (`src/lib/plans.ts`)

Single source of truth for the `Plan` enum + commercial config:

| Plan | Pricing | Leads/cycle | AI credits | Seats | Mockups |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| FREE | $0 | 50 | 20 | 1 | 3 |
| PRO | $79 / £59 | (see plans.ts) | (see) | (see) | (see) |
| PRO_TEAM | (see) | (see) | (see) | (see) | (see) |
| AGENCY | (see) | (see) | (see) | (see) | (see) |

Each plan has `priceIds: { USD, GBP }` and `annualPriceIds: { USD, GBP }` populated from env vars (e.g. `STRIPE_PRICE_PRO_USD`, `STRIPE_PRICE_PRO_GBP`, `STRIPE_PRICE_PRO_USD_ANNUAL`).

Helpers — use these, do not roll your own:

- `getPriceId(plan, currency, cycle)` — annual fallback to monthly fallback to USD
- `hasAnnualPricing(plan, currency)` — feature gate
- `getDisplayPrice(plan, currency, cycle)` — annual returns discounted per-month figure
- `currencySymbol(currency)` — `£` or `$`
- `normalizeCurrency`, `normalizeCycle` — narrow strings safely
- `detectBrowserCurrency()` — UK locales → GBP, else USD
- `getPlanLabel(plan)` — never render `"PRO_TEAM"` to users; this title-cases
- `planAllowsAdditionalSeat(plan, currentSeatCount)` — seat invite gate

## Webhook (`/api/billing/webhook`) — non-negotiable rules

```ts
export const runtime = "nodejs"; // required — needs raw body + Prisma
```

1. **Verify signature** against `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET`. 503 if not set, 400 if missing `stripe-signature`, 400 if `constructEvent` throws.
2. **Idempotency** via `prisma.stripeEventLog.create({ data: { id: eventId, type } })`. Catch `P2002` = duplicate, return 200 immediately.
3. Use `request.text()` — Stripe needs the raw body. Don't `request.json()`.
4. Detect plan from price id via `detectPlanFromPriceId(priceId)` (matches against `PLANS[*].priceIds.{USD,GBP}`).
5. Notify the workspace via `notifyBillingEvent` for human-relevant events.

## Test/live key separation

- `.env.local` carries test keys; production env carries live. Never commit either.
- Webhook secret in dev: `stripe listen --forward-to localhost:3000/api/billing/webhook` produces a `whsec_*` test secret.
- Currency-specific env vars: `STRIPE_PRICE_PRO_USD`, `STRIPE_PRICE_PRO_GBP`. Annual variants suffix `_ANNUAL`.

## Plan gating

Two enforcement layers:

1. **API route** — call `assertWorkerQuota({ workspaceId, kind })` (from `src/lib/agent-workers/quota.ts`) before queueing AI work. 402 with upsell payload if exceeded.
2. **Worker process** — `executeAgentRun` re-asserts quota at job start. Defense in depth — direct queue enqueue must not bypass.

For non-AI features (seats, custom branding, public profiles), use `planMeetsMinimum(workspace.plan, requiredPlan)` and `planAllowsAdditionalSeat(plan, currentSeatCount)`.

## Cycle reset

The webhook updates `Workspace.currentPeriodEnd` and `Workspace.cycleResetAt` on `customer.subscription.updated` and `invoice.payment_succeeded`. UI meters read `cycleResetAt` for the "resets on X" copy — don't recompute from `current_period_end` elsewhere.

## Downgrade handling

When a workspace downgrades (e.g. PRO → FREE):

1. Webhook updates `Workspace.plan`.
2. Existing `AgentRun` rows in flight finish under their original quota.
3. New runs gate against the new plan automatically (quota helper reads `Workspace.plan` live).
4. Seat overage: do NOT auto-revoke memberships; the UI surfaces "X seats over plan limit, downgrade to keep N" — owner action required.

## Failed payments / dunning

Currently relies on Stripe's built-in dunning + customer portal. The `customer.subscription.updated` webhook flips plan to FREE when subscription enters `unpaid`/`canceled`. We notify the owner via `notifyBillingEvent`.

## Refunds & disputes

- Refund: handled in Stripe dashboard; webhook delivers `charge.refunded` — log it but do not auto-revoke access mid-cycle.
- Dispute: `charge.dispute.created` → notify ops, freeze workspace if needed (manual decision).

## Customer portal

`POST /api/billing/portal` creates a Stripe billing portal session. Reuses `Workspace.stripeCustomerId` — do not let users have multiple Stripe customers per workspace.

## Anti-patterns

- ❌ Pinning `apiVersion` in `new Stripe(...)`
- ❌ Reading raw body with `request.json()` in the webhook (signature fails)
- ❌ Looking up plan from a string passed in the request — derive from `priceId` via `detectPlanFromPriceId`
- ❌ Skipping `StripeEventLog` dedup — Stripe DOES retry delivered events
- ❌ Hardcoded prices in UI — read from `PLANS` + `getDisplayPrice`
- ❌ Letting `getStripe()` throw at module load — call it only when needed (lazy singleton already handles this)
